{"name":"Princess Peach","hex":"#f878f8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"princess","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female member of a royal family other than a queen, especially a daughter or granddaughter of a monarch. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A woman or girl who excels in a given field or class."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/princess"},{"term":"peach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tree of species Prunus persica, native to China and now widely cultivated throughout temperate regions, having pink flowers and edible fruit.","Soft juicy stone fruit of the peach tree, having yellow flesh, downy, red-tinted yellow skin, and a deeply sculptured pit or stone containing a single seed."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the color peach.","Particularly pleasing or agreeable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Princess Peach","blocks":[{"text":"Princess Peach  is a character in Nintendo's Mario franchise. She was created by Shigeru Miyamoto and introduced in the 1985 original Super Mario Bros. game as Princess Toadstool. She is the princess regnant and head of state of the Mushroom Kingdom, where she resides in her castle along with Toads. Since her debut, she has appeared in the majority of Mario video games as the main female character and the romantic interest of Mario."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/16/Princess_Peach_Stock_Art.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Peach"},{"title":"Princess","blocks":[{"text":"Princess is a title used by a female member of a regnant monarch's family or by a female ruler of a principality. The male equivalent is a prince. Most often, the term has been used for the consort of a prince, or for the daughter of a monarch. A crown princess can be the heir apparent to the throne or the spouse of the heir apparent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg/330px-Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess"},{"title":"Peach","blocks":[{"text":"The peach is a deciduous tree that bears edible juicy fruits with various characteristics. Most are simply called peaches, while the glossy-skinned, non-fuzzy varieties are called nectarines. Though from the same species, they are regarded commercially as different fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg/330px-Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach"},{"title":"Peach (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Peach is a color that is named for the pale color of the interior flesh of the peach fruit. Like the color apricot, the color peach is paler than most actual peach fruits and seems to have been formulated primarily to create a pastel palette of colors for interior design."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Shigeru_Miyamoto_20150610_%28cropped_2%29.jpg/500px-Shigeru_Miyamoto_20150610_%28cropped_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Shigeru_Miyamoto_20150610_%28cropped_2%29.jpg/500px-Shigeru_Miyamoto_20150610_%28cropped_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shigeru Miyamoto, 2015","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShigeru_Miyamoto_20150610_(cropped_2).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/82/Princess_Peach_Kotabe_illustration.jpg/330px-Princess_Peach_Kotabe_illustration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/82/Princess_Peach_Kotabe_illustration.jpg/330px-Princess_Peach_Kotabe_illustration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustrations of Princess Peach drawn by Yōichi Kotabe","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APrincess_Peach_Kotabe_illustration.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Anya_Taylor-Joy_%2829787630588%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Anya_Taylor-Joy_%2829787630588%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Anya_Taylor-Joy_%2829787630588%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Anya_Taylor-Joy_%2829787630588%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Anya_Taylor-Joy_%2829787630588%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Anya_Taylor-Joy_%2829787630588%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anya Taylor-Joy voices Princess Peach in The Super Mario Bros. Movie and The Super Mario Galaxy Movie.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnya_Taylor-Joy_(29787630588)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Princess_Benedikte_of_Denmark_-2.jpg/500px-Princess_Benedikte_of_Denmark_-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Princess_Benedikte_of_Denmark_-2.jpg/500px-Princess_Benedikte_of_Denmark_-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Princess Benedikte of Denmark wearing insignia of the Order of the Polar Star (Sweden) and various Danish orders' insignia while in Stockholm, 2013","link":"